+## Secret — Fatal Exception, milestone B
+
+B adds `desktop` 9000 / `breakdown` 8000 / `stop` 5000 ms to A's 10000 ms. The temporary release remains 600 ms plus the existing 400 ms direct flip: 33000 ms total at Normal and 23100 ms at Fast, excluding charge. The authored 40-second film remains C work. Its spec stays in `alpha-updates/2.3.0-secret-cutscene/SPEC.md`.
+
+`secret-os-scene.js` owns the tiny procedural desktop model and rasterization. All randomness comes from the reserved serial, separate from pull RNG. The dialog bank, scene timing, OS palette, buffer sizes, window caps and profile choreography live in `src/data/secret-cutscene.js`. The painter reads the shared runtime's presentation clock; Safe admissions and 120 ms entrances use real playback milliseconds instead of canonical story time. Scrub/Fast cannot exceed twelve admissions in a rolling second. Registered section jumps now include desktop/breakdown/stop.
+
+The screen engine's ping-pong buffers store nearest-sampled raw OS pixels at OS resolution. A persistent mask preserves swept hung-window footprints, while healthy/current windows draw through. CRT shading, noise and bloom are applied once after feedback, avoiding darkening history. The scene keeps a masked Canvas mirror for context failure and scales it when quality drops. Low draws bounded historical poses; Mono converts both GPU and Canvas output. Existing shared warm-up, adaptive quality, skip, hidden pause, recovery and direct flip are reused.
+
+D features original icons, the autonomous arrow/hourglass, exponential errors, NORTH, Task Manager's pegged CPU/off-chart memory graph, accelerating Explorer, a defrag map and SECRET clipboard. Diagnostic windows get readable beats before the avalanche buries them. E introduces four era treatments, year progression, detached falling icons, disappearing bars, block tears, held tiles displaced by cursor motion and static/pulsed VRAM patches. High adds sorting/8x8 quantization; Medium omits them. Full allows at most four 350 ms artifact bursts in E, inside 500 ms globally gated bursts; Safe uses fixed irregular low-contrast patches and 800 ms theme crossfades. Full checker patches appear only outside bursts. Safe shake is capped at 3 px and 2.5 Hz.
+
+F shows the original blue stop screen, backward progress and a deliberately non-QR fragment grid. Safe reboots once over 1500 ms; Full has three faster attempts, with rapid cuts restricted to the first allowed burst and later attempts blended. The console then types reveal/denied/override/force and scrolls seeded hex with repeated `53 45 43 52 45 54`. Scene-generated error/themeFlip/reboot beats join descriptor beats through the shared exact-once runtime, rather than emitting from a private loop. B releases the terminal into A's field; G/H and full Short/calm/background choreography remain C.
